    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bb7b2ae_7bdfe399",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_discovery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T18:16:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This changes the behavior in the case that the received SVDM version is greater than 2.1, which I don\u0027t think was the intent for this CL.\n\nThe only use of this field that I see right now is to control DPAM VDM construction/parsing. IIRC, the intent of this logic is to store the highest SVDM version that we have in common with the partner/cable. If we saw, e.g. 3.0, we\u0027d want to store 2.1, because that\u0027s the highest version this code understands.\n\nI think the previous logic is also wrong. If we saw 3.1, we\u0027d store 2.1, but if we saw 3.0, we\u0027d store 2.0. That doesn\u0027t make any sense.\n\nI\u0027d suggest fixing the logic in a CL preceding this one, then changing to a `switch` statement as a no-op refactor.",
      "revId": "098170f943e69ccdb41a7b2538350de3279a3d65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5cf23af4_9600f073",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_discovery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1131142
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T18:39:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This actually looks right to me as we were seeing Major 2 Minor 1 and Major 2 Minor 0 before. Now that they are unified it seems correct to just always set version to passed in version if it exists. I have to double check on the values here though cause I think before we were setting 0x10 with SVDM_VER_2_1 and now it\u0027s setting 0x0101 so the code should be updated just havent had a chance to go through the whole patch yet.\n\nIf I\u0027m looking at this correctly even the default case could just be the same assignment (but if nothing is returned I can see the issue there). The main key here is that since the mask is now changed we just directly set the full value.",
      "parentUuid": "4bb7b2ae_7bdfe399",
      "revId": "098170f943e69ccdb41a7b2538350de3279a3d65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8c153f1_47d63e9f",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_discovery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T20:14:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I have to double check on the values here though cause I think before we were setting 0x10 with SVDM_VER_2_1 and now it\u0027s setting 0x0101 so the code should be updated just havent had a chance to go through the whole patch yet.\n\nThis CL changes the enum values of `SVDM_VER_2_1`, etc. to also contain the minor version. Before, they only had the major version, and the minor version was a separate field. So for 2.1, 0b01 \u003d\u003e 0b0101.\n\n\u003e This actually looks right to me as we were seeing Major 2 Minor 1 and Major 2 Minor 0 before.\n\nTBC, I think the happy path (partner has VDM version 2.1) is still correct and the same. I think it changes the behavior in the case where the version number is one we\u0027ve never seen before, from the future.",
      "parentUuid": "5cf23af4_9600f073",
      "revId": "098170f943e69ccdb41a7b2538350de3279a3d65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
