      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T10:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(not done yet...)\n\nTable 5-5 only uses the DPAM version field. It\u0027s possible that a port supports SVDM2.1 + DPAM2.0.\n\nThe footnotes below also mentions this scenario.\n\n\u003e b. If Initiator and Responder both support SVDM Version 2.1 or higher and if either Initiator or Responder supports DPAM\nVersion 2.0 or earlier, then all DP Capabilities exchange shall follow DisplayPort Alt Mode on USB Type-C specification 2.0\nor earlier.",
      "parentUuid": "17441063_a6f43545",
      "revId": "098170f943e69ccdb41a7b2538350de3279a3d65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b077848_f28dc050",
        "filename": "common/usbc/dp_alt_mode.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141739
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T10:39:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My interpretation of the spec is that SVDM version only indicates the existence of DPAM field. (SVDM2.1 does not imply DPAM 2.1)\n\nTable 5-6, footnote j:\n\u003e If SVDM Version is 2.1 or higher, DPAM Version field is applicable else this field shall be set to 00b.",
      "parentUuid": "c68fb307_788d008d",
      "revId": "098170f943e69ccdb41a7b2538350de3279a3d65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
